const limits=`- **VERIFIED_OPEN — production access requests (P1):** The 17 October Staff account/password panel reported unavailable. Login worked in that observed session. Generic 503 does not establish schema, grants or another storage cause; a scoped log query was empty. No accessible production Studio session was available in the 19 October browser inventory, so no new private check is claimed. Read-only repository environment discovery found only the example and isolated QA configuration, with no production database connection available for schema/grant diagnosis.
- **VERIFIED_OPEN — released mobile performance (P2):** All four 17 October mobile cold-browser LCP medians exceed 2.5 seconds; three finite search tasks exceed 200 ms. These are lab observations, not field INP. The candidate remains local.
- **${stressStatus} — historical local navigation stress:** ${stressText}
- **DEFERRED — development dependency advisory (P2):** Production-only audit is clear, but the full audit retains ${devEntries} entries caused by ${devAdvisories.length} braces advisory. No patched upstream release existed on 19 October. Keep lint configuration trusted; avoid an incompatible downgrade. Read [SECURITY-RELEASE-REVIEW.md](SECURITY-RELEASE-REVIEW.md).
- **BLOCKED — field acceptance:** Existing Vercel p75 LCP/INP/CLS queries for 16 October 00:00–17 October 06:00 UTC returned empty arrays. No percentile, zero-value inference or new tracking installation is claimed.
- **BLOCKED — native/device acceptance:** No physical phone/tablet is available. Narrator exists, but no observed spoken task was available through supported controls; no new reader was installed. Native 200%/400% browser zoom remains unexecuted; browser reflow is separate evidence.
- **BLOCKED — private provider bytes:** Isolated QA has no remote Blob token. Metadata authorization is tested; actual upload/download/deletion bytes need a dedicated nonproduction provider.
- **DEFERRED — lifecycle and conditional breadth:** Full erasure/replay and fresh publication/rollback write matrices need wholly disposable records/storage. Source-only locale/legacy redirects, loading/error boundaries, child path/create contracts and optional homepage/landing variants remain scoped in the inventory. Production role inheritance and every permission combination are not proven.
- **DEFERRED — scale and human judgement:** Translation-list scaling needs timing. Mixed-language FAQ/collection/related-card/story-rail boundaries remain source-review candidates, not newly proved bugs or complete assistive certification. Independent meaning, factual/media permission and physical acceptance require actual human evidence. Historical administrator acceptance is not new independent proof.
- **INTENTIONAL — exclusions:** No customer checkout/accounts, new scraping, legacy transfers, removed backups or inactive prerequisite services were activated. No new design direction, motion/UI package, tracker or stock media was added. Existing dependency versions were patched for security.`;
await writeFile(`${root}/FINAL-VERIFICATION.md`,`# Final verification — 17–19 October 2026\n\nThis is a completed audit and a locally verified candidate, **not a production release or complete accessibility/performance certification**.\n\n- Production base: 66e82ef04f76b8460654bab4329ccbadfb47f28e, Vercel READY deployment dpl_7u2Yji4v5cpAbPde4DRq3Ua1LfDw and its production alias rechecked read-only on 19 October (release-identity-2026-10-19.json). Broad public/private browser evidence remains dated 17 October; no new private Studio session was available on 19 October.\n- Local branch: ${branch}; preserved acceptance checkpoint 40907ff. Application content fingerprint: ${fingerprint.applicationSha256}. The later final local commit is reported in Git/the handoff; no circular self-SHA is embedded.\n- ${fixed.length} issue-register fixes verified locally; ${open.length} verified open issues; ${deferred.length} deferred investigations; ${notReproduced.length} not reproduced in the latest bounded retest. Fixed status means the candidate passed its listed checks; production remains unchanged.\n\n${tests}\n\n## Execution details and honest limits\n\nPreserved 17 October broad evidence used Chrome 155.0.8059.40; final 19 October targeted runs used Chrome ${studio.browser}. DPR 1. Widths: 1920, 1440, 1200, 992, 768, 512, 390, 320. Normal heights: 1000 desktop / 1024 tablet / 844 mobile; short cases 320 × 480 and 390 × 568. Baseline responsive and conditional suites ran before the narrow audit patch; subsequent checks target changed behavior, all canonical E2E contracts and the 86 accessibility combinations. Not all ${layouts.rows.length} screenshots were manually reviewed. The broad matrix was not silently relabelled as a post-dependency-patch rerun.\n\nLint exits 0 with 62 existing warnings (lint.log); no blanket warning-free claim. The final application build, type and runtime checks pass. The first post-patch unit attempt failed one obsolete exact-version assertion expecting Next 16.3.5; its log and checks.previousAttempts were retained. The expected pin was updated to 16.3.8 and the final run passed. Initial obsolete home E2E 500 and later fixture-loader failure are retained as before/diagnostic evidence; the final ${e2e.stats.expected}-pass run is separately identified. The 17 October E2E log contained five stream-close notices; the final 19 October run contained two, plus color and external lockfile warnings. No tested request/page-error assertion failed. ${stressText}\n\nThe workflow restores all new disposable test rows and compares 21-table fingerprints within its run. Authentication metadata and identity-sequence advances are excluded. A separate original audit-start/final post-patch snapshot verifies all ${protectedRows} protected original records across ${protectedScopes} scopes byte-identically. This is **local QA preservation**, not a live database comparison.\n\n## Remaining gates\n\n${limits}\n\n## Independent reviews\n\n[SECURITY-RELEASE-REVIEW.md](SECURITY-RELEASE-REVIEW.md) records dependency applicability, registry compatibility and independent application-diff review. [FINAL-REVIEW-NOTES.md](FINAL-REVIEW-NOTES.md) records independent evidence reconciliation and its subsequent report corrections. Reviews supplement executable checks and do not authorize release.\n\n## Evidence and release boundary\n\nRaw screenshots, traces, JSON receipts, HTML reports and the local [gallery](../../../test-results/rivya-master-audit/index.html) are ignored by Git. Only sanitized reports/tools/tests/source may enter a future PR. See [ISSUE-REGISTER.csv](ISSUE-REGISTER.csv) for reproduction and source details. **No push, PR, merge, deployment, production data mutation or CMS publication was performed.** Obtain fresh explicit authorization only after a concrete production repair/release plan is reviewed.\n`);
await writeFile(`${root}/IMPLEMENTATION-ROADMAP.md`,`# Implementation roadmap — 17–19 October 2026 and production gate\n\n## Completed locally\n\nRetained the released cinematic design and isolated the existing acceptance bundle in 40907ff. Reproduced and corrected narrowly scoped memory/pause, content language, filter semantics, leave confirmation, table focus, pagination, related-section continuity, date validation, note accuracy and current E2E/documentation defects. No schema, stored product/content/crop/published-revision data or business information changed. Existing Next and matched lint config were patched to 16.3.8, Sharp to 0.35.5 and transitive source-map-js to 1.2.2; no new direct dependency or framework major migration was introduced.\n\n## 1. Restore the production account/recovery queue — P1\n\nThe concrete failure is the Staff access-request panel, not a failed administrator login. Read-only diagnosis is already authorized and should inspect existence, columns/indexes and runtime-role privileges for rivya_access_requests, the related token/staff structures and the exact deployed service query. Compare against [schema](../../../scripts/studio-access-migration.sql) and [least-privilege grants](../../../scripts/studio-access-runtime-grants.sql). Do not run a broad migration on the strength of the generic UI error. Existing read-only runtime logs did not establish cause. Current repository environment discovery found only the example and isolated QA configuration; no production database connection or accessible production Studio session was available on 19 October. Diagnosis is authorized but needs appropriate existing read access.\n\nIf a schema/grant discrepancy is verified, prepare only the required additive SQL, record before/after schema and runtime-role evidence, and present it for **fresh explicit production authorization**. Preserve all staff/password/version/request rows. Validate schema twice in a disposable local database first. Following authorized repair, re-open Staff and test only separately authorized synthetic request/recovery records, including approval, expiry, one-use redemption and revoked-session handling. The user enters actual credentials in Studio.\n\n## 2. Candidate release review\n\nReview this branch and full acceptance baseline separately from protected business data. Recheck production main/deployment drift, pass exact candidate checks and prepare a detailed PR only after fresh authorization. No production promotion or publication follows automatically from local verification. After an approved release, confirm exact main SHA/READY alias, public routes/media, translated schema and private Staff/media/permissions. Until then all candidate fixes are local.\n\n## 3. Performance follow-up — P2\n\nUse the measured tables in [PERFORMANCE-AND-SEO.md](PERFORMANCE-AND-SEO.md). Compare the deployed candidate under the same three cold + one repeat profiles, with browser caches distinguished from uncontrolled server/CDN caches. Attribute the slow collection TTFB sample and homepage LCP/font/video phases. Retain publication/withdrawal consistency; no aggressive cache redesign is authorized by these measurements. Collect legitimate existing field observations; missing p75 is not acceptance.\n\nThe full dependency audit retains ${devEntries} package entries from ${devAdvisories.length} development-only braces advisory. No compatible patched upstream release was available on 19 October. Keep lint configuration trusted; evaluate an upstream patch when published without an incompatible lint-config downgrade. This report creates no monitoring automation.\n\n## 4. Dedicated nonproduction lifecycle QA\n\nProvision or designate a wholly disposable DB and private media store before destructive erasure/provider-deletion/CMS rollback testing. Inventory and retain original protected records in the existing QA database. Do not reuse production tokens or send a WhatsApp message. Measure translation overview transfer/DOM/filter latency before proposing summary/pagination changes.\n\n## 5. Historical local catalogue navigation stress\n\nReproduce studio-regressions-same-page.json with normal user link navigation and fresh versus warm optimizer cache. Capture sanitized pending request source/size/timing, browser connection and local server diagnostics. The historical failure followed repeated width changes/pagination; ordinary independent editor navigation succeeds. Do not infer a production outage or replace Next Image without tracing cause. ${stressText} Preserve the archived 17 October failure and the final retest separately.\n\n## 6. Human/device acceptance\n\nUse actual phones/tablets and an existing supported screen reader when available. Record browser/OS/device and concrete tasks: navigation, media pause, filter/search, validation, unsaved draft cancel, access request and recovery; native 200%/400% zoom, short heights and long translations. Independently review native-language meaning and provenance where still missing. No physical device was offered for this audit, and installing a new screen reader is outside the chosen permission.\n\n## Decision\n\nThe audit and safe local fixes are reviewable. The production system is **not unconditionally ready for sign-off** because the access-request feature is unavailable, mobile performance targets are missed, the development-only advisory is deferred and external evidence gates remain. The final local stress status is ${stressStatus}. None is silently relabeled as an administrator-completed test.\n`);
await writeFile(`${root}/EXECUTIVE-SUMMARY.md`,`# Rivya full website, Studio and codebase audit\n\n**17–19 October 2026 — audit delivery complete within the documented scope; targeted local fixes verified; production sign-off withheld.** The main remaining production issues are an unavailable account/password-request queue and cold mobile performance above the requested target. ${stressText} Existing dependencies were also patched locally; the development-only braces advisory remains deferred. No release or production mutation was performed.\n\n## 1. Scope and Git baseline\n\nAudited the current app, published production pages, authenticated Studio, shared systems, workflow/privacy contracts, eight responsive widths, motion/media, accessibility and performance. Started at 66e82ef04f76b8460654bab4329ccbadfb47f28e (PR #63), following cinematic PR #62 (224b2ca0e192b8d8ceced3045d6f8a193b734362). Both release records were read. Main and the exact Vercel READY production alias were rechecked on 19 October; the private Studio opening survey remains from 17 October. Branch: ${branch}. Pre-existing local acceptance work was preserved in 40907ff before new fixes. Application fingerprint: ${fingerprint.applicationSha256}. Sources/ mirror remains read-only.\n\n## 2. Existing completed features retained\n\nKept the existing logo/palette, serif hierarchy, shared cursor lighting, viewport-based storytelling, seamless homepage sections, Hero/Resin poster-first parallax films, reduced-motion controls, public templates, Studio 37 workspaces, revisions, translations, protected inquiry workflow and manual WhatsApp boundary. This audit did not repeat the cinematic redesign.\n\n## 3. Main website results\n\nThe 17 October production inventory checked 656 published sitemap URLs for HTTP 200, title and H1, and 246 referenced asset HEAD responses. This proves availability at the audit time, not every per-record interaction. Local layouts cover 73 distinct route instances and representative dynamic templates; metadata, language fallbacks, public error states, search/filter/sort, saved pieces and customization are covered through source and targeted/browser suites. No claim that every possible content combination is tested. A small 19 October read-only refresh separately returned HTTP 200 for the homepage, Studio sign-in, robots and sitemap; it does not replace the 17 October full inventory (public-availability-2026-10-19.json).\n\n## 4. Studio/admin results\n\nOn 17 October, all 37 registered production destinations were opened using the owner-renewed session. No accessible production Studio session was available for a 19 October recheck. Initial openings had no horizontal overflow/completed broken-image flags; a later settled Staff panel revealed **PROD-ACCESS-01 (P1)**. Page openings are therefore not reported as full-module passes. Local conditional coverage exercised 321 states/1051 checks across editors, child controls, saved layouts and intercepted failure states. Actual roles/persistence/recovery were tested separately with new fictional local records. Inactive import/subscriber prerequisites and excluded scraping/fill features remain inactive/absent.\n\n## 5. Section-by-section observations\n\n| Family | Decision and observed treatment |\n|---|---|\n| Homepage Hero and Resin in Motion | KEEP viewport-based full-bleed video, approved posters/captions and independent pause controls; fix low-memory and paused CSS movement. |\n| Introduction, material/story chapters, worlds and closing invitation | KEEP continuous dark gradients and editorial compositions; no new fullscreen forcing or asset substitution. |\n| Featured collection, categories and galleries | KEEP responsive natural grids and media framing; product-related gradient edge corrected locally. |\n| Portfolio, testimonials, FAQ and landing blocks | KEEP factual labels, concept/sample provenance and content-led growth. All 19 home slots/16 landing block types are source-inventoried; runtime evidence varies by actual fixture. |\n| Article/brand/process/care/legal pages | KEEP long-form natural height and readable overlays; correct effective content-language metadata and English fallback boundaries. |\n| Commission/contact/customization | KEEP practical forms and consent/manual-send workflow. Never lock long forms to 100vh. |\n| Navigation, footer, unavailable and loading states | KEEP shared semantics and brand; tested focus, Escape, responsive menu and poster/error fallbacks. |\n| Studio access | KEEP approved image/logo/frosted panel; finite contrast samples verified, not every animation frame. |\n| Studio operational/editor pages | KEEP compact functional data layouts; fix filters, return guard, keyboard comparison and pagination. |\n\n[ROUTE-STUDIO-INVENTORY.csv](ROUTE-STUDIO-INVENTORY.csv) contains 230 source-to-component/data/access/state rows with fresh runtime evidence annotations where available.\n\n## 6. Legacy comparison\n\n[DESIGN-COMPARISON.md](DESIGN-COMPARISON.md) records KEEP/IMPROVE/DO NOT COPY against the old public site and Era reference. The 17 October set of 38 reference captures distinguish settled views from preloaders. Kept current brand/media/architecture; did not copy external assets, navigation/services, bright palettes, preloader delays or old backend behavior. Earlier Bionis/Medesk/Gridline pattern adaptations and their [MIT notice](../../redesign/CRAFT-THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.md) remain intact. No new dashboard source/component was copied during this audit.\n\n## 7. Responsive screenshot coverage\n\n${layouts.rows.length} preserved 17 October local observations: 73 routes × 1920/1440/1200/992/768/512/390/320, plus four short-height cases. Chrome 155.0.8059.40, DPR 1. Baseline capture found 0 horizontal overflow flags/0 execution errors. All images are indexed in a local navigable gallery; selected representative captures received visual inspection, not all 588. Narrow after-fix captures and behavior checks are paired only when actually available.\n\n## 8. Accessibility\n\nThe final post-patch automated run has ${axe.rows.length} scans across 43 families/two widths, with ${axe.rows.flatMap(r=>r.violations).length} detected violations and ${axe.errors.length} execution errors. Fixed the comparison scroll-region keyboard failure, filter semantics and fallback language boundaries. ${contrast.samples.length} preserved 17 October finite rendered contrast samples passed across five video times, ambient positions and labelled white/black media stresses; ${interactions.checks.length} preserved interaction/fallback checks passed. These do not constitute native-reader certification, every video-frame contrast certification or physical-device acceptance.\n\n## 9. Performance and SEO\n\nProduction desktop cold LCP medians were 1712/1120/1064/956 ms for home/collection/journal/product. Mobile medians were 4804/2788/3604/2620 ms under CPU 4×, 150 ms latency, 1.6 Mbps down. One collection TTFB was 3757 ms, with other cold samples 48/58 ms; median alone conceals it. Mobile search-task maxima were 424/224/152/208 ms; finite lab tasks are not field INP. Cold CLS remained below 0.001. Existing field LCP/INP/CLS queries returned no observations. Full production/local tables, resource totals and caveats appear in [PERFORMANCE-AND-SEO.md](PERFORMANCE-AND-SEO.md). Production hi/gu Article schema language mismatch is reproduced and locally render-tested fixed; deployed output remains unchanged.\n\n## 10. Functional/security/privacy results\n\n${workflow.checks.length} final 19 October local assertions pass: current product/variant validation, persistence/idempotency/concurrency, receipt ownership/recovery, assignment and role checks, stale conflicts, origin checks, private-reference metadata authorization, access approval/one-time redemption, recovery and session revocation. Corrected follow-up audit-note accuracy and calendar validation, including rejection of year zero before PostgreSQL casting. No customer inquiry or external message was invented or sent. All 1,658 original protected records across 13 scopes are identical from audit start to the final snapshot; no production-data preservation claim is inferred from local hashes. Private-provider bytes and destructive lifecycle tests remain separate gates. Next/matched lint config 16.3.8, Sharp 0.35.5 and source-map-js 1.2.2 clear the production-only dependency audit. The full audit retains ${devEntries} entries from ${devAdvisories.length} development-only braces advisory. [SECURITY-RELEASE-REVIEW.md](SECURITY-RELEASE-REVIEW.md) records actual applicability, registry compatibility and official advisory links; no exploit or production rollout is claimed.\n\n## 11. Issue register\n\n${fixed.length} locally verified fixes, ${open.length} verified open issues, ${deferred.length} deferred investigations and ${notReproduced.length} historical stress finding not reproduced in the latest bounded retest. No confirmed P0 in the executed scope. [ISSUE-REGISTER.csv](ISSUE-REGISTER.csv) includes severity, viewport, actual/expected, reproduction, source, evidence, risk, effort, validation and final status. The locally remediated dependency finding is P1; the production request panel remains P1. Released mobile performance remains P2. The development advisory is deferred P2; local stress is ${stressStatus}.\n\n## 12. Implementation roadmap\n\n[IMPLEMENTATION-ROADMAP.md](IMPLEMENTATION-ROADMAP.md) orders production read-only diagnosis, a concrete additive repair plan for fresh authorization, candidate release review, deployed performance retest, disposable provider/lifecycle QA and genuine native/device acceptance. No broad redesign or speculative optimization is queued as a completed fix.\n\n## 13. Exact tests\n\n${tests}\n\n## 14. Outstanding gates\n\n${limits}\n\n## 15. Git and release-readiness conclusion\n\nThe source, focused tests and ten requested report files are local on ${branch}; raw screenshots/traces/private evidence remain ignored. No push, PR, merge, deploy, production business-data write or CMS publication occurred. All current original brand/content/media/database contracts were preserved in the tested scope. **Audit delivery is complete; unconditional production acceptance is not.** Read [FINAL-VERIFICATION.md](FINAL-VERIFICATION.md) before any release decision.\n`);
